  "id": "classification-table",
  "term": "classification table",
  "definition": "A classification table is a structured way of organizing multiple clinical dimensions so they can be considered together in an assessment. In this context, it helps combine areas such as symptom severity, functional limits, daily functioning, clinical coherence, and work demands into a clearer, more transparent summary.",
